  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the resale value of a Hyundai Creta in India?",
      "a": "A well-maintained Creta retains approximately 78% of its ex-showroom price after two years, 71% after three years, and 56% after five years. For a 2022 SX petrol with 25,000 to 50,000 km, the current fair-market band is roughly ₹10.12 to ₹11.64 lakh."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the Creta hold value better than the Kia Seltos?",
      "a": "Yes, by a meaningful margin. The Creta retains about 71% at three years versus roughly 63% for the Seltos, driven by Hyundai's larger service network and the Creta's longer brand history in India. In smaller metros and tier-2 cities, the gap can widen further in Creta's favour."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is a diesel Creta a good used-car buy?",
      "a": "Yes, particularly for buyers with high annual mileage (above 15,000 km per year) or those outside NCR. The 1.5L CRDi engine has a strong reliability record, and diesel Creta trades 6 to 9% above equivalent petrol in most metros. In NCR, factor in the 10-year diesel cutoff before buying pre-2017 cars."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which is the best city to sell a Creta?",
      "a": "Bengaluru currently trades at approximately +5% above the national mid, followed by Mumbai at +4%. Chennai, Delhi NCR and Hyderabad are all at +2 to +3%. Kolkata is soft at −2%."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much does a Creta depreciate per year?",
      "a": "Roughly 13% in year one, 9% additional in year two, 7% in year three, and 7 to 8% per year through year five. The five-year retention of 56% is 5 percentage points above the mid-SUV segment average of 51%."
    }
  ],
